<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10275" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">con-glŏmĕro</span></b> , no <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>perf.</i>,
				ātum, 1, v. a. (very rare),
				<i>to roll together, wind up, conglomerate</i>.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop., * <i><span class="en">Lucr. 3,
			211</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">venae intortae et conglomeratae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels.
					7, 18 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			— * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to crowd, heap</i>,
			or <i>press together</i>: omnia mala in
			aliquem, Enn. ap <i><span class="en">Non. p. 90, 15</span></i> (Trag.
			Rel. v. 307 Rib.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
